 ° Registration Information °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°
ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

As a software developer, I take pride in my efforts to produce high
quality shareware.  In order to do so, some of my software requires a
small registration fee.

The John Dailey Software products are being released under the Shareware
concept, which encourages the users of a program to register that
software after a trial period of approximately 60 days and continued use
thereafter.

To encourage registration, some elements of the software not required
for it to work properly may have been disabled.  Please refer to the
product documentation for information on registration features.

By registering and supporting quality shareware such as this, you are
making the John Dailey Software products bigger, better, and more
enjoyable for you and your users.

Upon receipt of your registration you will receive a unique, individual
registration code(s) (with instructions), which is easily used to make
the software executable registered.  Registration of the John Dailey
Software products entitle you to FREE UPDATES of the same major version
number, i.e. 1.x, 2.x, etc.  All you'll need to do is acquire the update
software package and incorporate your registration code.

Registration will also activate all registered-only features of the
program and remove all unregistered delays and nag screens.  Your name
and registration number will also appear to you (and your users if
applicable) as the game is executed.

If you are unhappy with any part of this John Dailey Software product,
either with it's operation, or the software itself, please do not send
in your registration expecting it to function more to your liking. 
Remember that the great concept of shareware is "try before you buy." 
You know exactly what you will receive before you pay for it.

If you are having problems, please don't hesitate to contact me before
giving up or registering the software.  I fully support the software for
anyone whether they have or have not registered.

All of the John Dailey Software products may be registered for both
sysop BBS and personal use.  If you don't operate a BBS, you can still
register many of the John Dailey Software game products for your own
personal enjoyment.

You may recieve your registration information via US Postal mail or e-
mail.  As well, you may have the software mailed to you on disk for a
small additional fee.  All of the John Dailey Software products can
currently be registered via pre-paid check or money order in US funds
only.  Individuals that prefer may register any John Dailey Software
product using their credit card by this form or online by visiting
www.johndaileysoftware.com or calling BBS Avalon at (407) 654-9705 24
hours a day, 7 days a week.  Upon reaching the main menu of the bulletin
board system, go to the John Dailey Software menu and press "O" for on-
line registration.  Registration codes are given usually within 24 hours
using this method of registration.

Credit card registrations are processed by Online Financial Services and
will appear on your bill as such.


To register your copy with this form, follow these easy steps:

     o    Print out the enclosed registration form (or print the
          information on paper).  Please include seperate registration
          forms for each order if you will be making multiple
          registrations.

     o    COMPLETELY and ledgibly fill out ALL information on the form. 
          Leaving any part of the form blank may delay your
          registration.

     o    Select which product or products you wish to register, and be
          sure to mark which discount you'd like if registering multiple
          products.

     o    Select which form of shipping and handling you prefer; postal
          mail, FidoNET or Internet e-mail, or by private e-mail on BBS
          Avalon.

     o    If you are having your registration code sent via the postal
          service, be sure to check whether or not you wish to recieve
          the software on disk along with your registration keycode.

     o    Total up the registration price, enclose a check or money
          order (do not send cash) in US funds payable to John Dailey if
          not paying by credit card, and mail your registration fee with
          the form to the address at the bottom of the form.
